ABSTRACTS={'A1-exact-benchmarks':'We construct a target-refined inverse-limit symplectic section for the generalized baker family, an exact autonomous Hamiltonian suspension on its smooth symplectic leaves, a global affine work connection, and a graded flag-current response calculus. The symbolic natural extension is the coupled map $(x,y)\\mapsto(\\sigma x,x_0y)$; no bilateral Koopman gap or independent past inverse is used.','A2-sinai-homological-pressure':'For the compact finite-horizon Lorentz family we build a parent-fold transfer bundle in which symbolic cut births are coordinate changes of one physical inverse branch. Returned-branch temporal nonintegrability, homological and collision-count periodic obstructions, a multi-block very-high-frequency estimate, and a gap-free Fourier partition yield a uniform vector--roof density and window local limit theorem.','A3-full-empirical-path-ldp':'The inducing process is treated directly as a countable Markov-renewal process stopped at deterministic collision or physical time. An entropy-control representation yields full good recurrent--recession path LDPs including unbounded excursion profiles, singularity exposure, and the pointed terminal residual. No cemetery Markovization or random speed is used.','A4-history-memory-universal-pressure':'We prove a weighted Harris--Doeblin theorem for the actual Sinai past kernel, derive a uniform quenched enhanced suspension invariance principle from the correctly centered Poisson martingale, construct the eigenfunction Doob nonlinear history semigroup, and obtain a normalized instantaneous--resonant--decaying memory decomposition from a continuous-time renewal resolvent with integrable vertical bounds.','B1-microcanonical-preparation':'Source-dependent microcanonical preparation is proved by a full complex-pressure Fourier theorem, not by spatially independent dynamical blocks. The singleton compound-Poisson pressure and the normally convergent trajectory-polymer remainder give Gaussian, compact-annulus, and speed-dependent high-frequency gaps. A degree-one finite saddle and a relative local theorem for regular CLT shells yield the constrained pressure and covariance Schur complement.','B2-collision-clusters-dynamic-ldp':'We construct the compatible space--time Green trace graph for deterministic hard spheres and control surplus contacts through the actual linearized collision map. Fixed-genealogy analytic transversality is summed by dominated convergence against factorial trajectory weights, avoiding a false genealogy-uniform exponent. Ovsyannikov source sewing, a continuous kinetic Hodge repair, and bounded-source exhaustion give the full density--actual-contact LDP and its microcanonical transfer.','B3-hamilton-boltzmann-cotangents':'On an explicit perturbative regular phase chart we prove a nonautonomous biased kinetic energy estimate. The covariance is constructed first from microscopic marked cumulants; its exact dual kernel follows from the initial-plus-collision Gaussian noise representation. The Cameron--Martin inverse has domain $\\operatorname{Ran}\\Sigma^{1/2}$, the action tangent is obtained by Mosco convergence, and process tightness retains the microscopic diagonal term.','B4-nonlinear-kinetic-semigroups':'Microscopic states, Koopman observables, pushed-forward laws, initial-law endpoint values, and the limiting action semigroup are kept distinct. A resolvent image of smooth reflected observables is a genuine generator core, and the full hierarchy corrector is solved in an exponential generating sequence space. The dynamic action is compared by primal verification along finite-entropy controls, avoiding uncontrolled exponential doubled jets.','C1-information-risk-sensitive-saddles':'Positive posterior slice measures are separated from oriented collision currents. A compact evidence-direction cone supplies the zero-evidence state, and integrated coarea disintegration gives a Feller belief kernel for definable observation strata. Inserted source-dependent coefficients, a predeclared analytic reachable-chaos class, belief dynamic programming, and an explicit controlled LAN/Bernstein--von Mises theorem follow.','C2-cotangent-rigidity-tangent-representations':'The weighted cotangent dual is the vector space of invariant signed Radon measures; invariant probabilities form its positive normalized slice. Equality of the full perturbed pressure functional is treated platform by platform. Transfer jets are typed on regularity levels, while physical memory uses a separate common-domain Hilbert form bundle. Optional projections and source versus state contraction derivatives are then rigorously separated.','D1-deterministic-theta-contractions':'We construct projectively compatible positive phase labels from peripheral positive bands of the microscopic platform operator, including an explicit complementary label. Normalized component pressures, phase-local LDPs, exact mixture rates, shell coefficients, Gaussian tangents, and dynamic semigroups are assembled on one joint labelled law. Phase costs are counted once and label contraction yields the nonconvex minimum rate.'}
